# LeakSanitizer suppressions for the instrumented HDF5/netCDF campaign (doc/fuzzing.md).
#
# netCDF-4's `nc_open` leaks the memory it allocated when it fails halfway through a
# corrupt file: the object-header buffer of `H5Gopen2` and the variable hash map it had
# already built (`NC_hashmapnew`). Both are inside the libraries and reproduce with the
# pinned netcdf-c and HDF5 on a one-byte mutation of a valid file (the "pipeline-copy
# leaks on failed dataset opens" class of the known library limitations), so the reader
# cannot free them. Only stacks that pass through `NC_open` are matched: a leak in
# meshio++'s own code is a bug to fix, never a line in this file.
leak:NC_open
